When I have decided I will never visit a branch again, I might
even roll a boulder over its entrance just so the stairs are
not visible.  Out of sight, out of mind.

Using a branch level early on is for richness of exploration
options.  Both the mines and sokoban are rich sources of items.
That's why I like to use one of those branch levels as an early
base camp.

But an altar does b/u/c id, so having an altar is even more
usefull for base camp than a branch level.  If any branch level
has an altar, it becomes my base camp for the rest of the game.
Mines, sokoban, ludios, quest, if any also have an altar it
becomes my base camp.

I like to use the room with an altar to b/u/c id items and
have a row on chests with labels like Ascension Kit, Armory,
Cursed Stuff, Treasure Chest and whatever else comes to mind.
Then I use an adjacent room if I want to polypile that game.

Also Valkyries have different options than other classes.
Other classes benefit from a deeper base camp because they
need to lug valuable stuff up to their camp.  Valks can use
the Orb of Fate to shuttle as much as they can carry each
descent.

